# Secrets
.env
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Data & models (keep structure via .gitkeep; don't commit large/raw/PII)
data/raw/*
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
data/gold/*
data/external/*
!**/.gitkeep
models/*
!models/.gitkeep

# ...but DO commit provenance.json (Phase 7).
# It is the traceability record and it never contains source text -- only
# licence basis, category, counts, and metadata. Committing it means a fresh
# clone can show what was ingested and under what basis without running
# anything, which is what the Phase 7 gate is actually about. The corpus itself
# stays out: data/raw/synth_precomp_v1/records.jsonl is regenerated
# deterministically by `python scripts/run_ingestion.py --seed 42`, so the seed
# is the reproducibility guarantee and the blob would just be history weight.
# Re-include the directories first -- git does not descend into an excluded dir --
# then re-exclude their contents, then carve out provenance.json.
!data/raw/*/
data/raw/*/*
!data/raw/*/provenance.json

# Same rule one layer down (Phase 8). `data/interim/` holds de-identified
# utterances, which are still corpus and still regenerable -- `python
# scripts/run_preprocessing.py` rebuilds them deterministically from data/raw/.
# What is committed is the evidence *about* that run: the derived provenance
# (which is where `deidentified: true` is recorded) and `preprocessing.json`
# (counts in, counts out, drop reasons, placeholder tallies). A fresh clone can
# then show what Phase 8 did without running anything, which is what the gate
# is actually about.
!data/interim/*/
data/interim/*/*
!data/interim/*/provenance.json
!data/interim/*/preprocessing.json

# Phase 9 gold-set candidates.
#
# The DRAWN CANDIDATE TEXT is derived data -- `scripts/run_eda.py` reproduces it
# byte-for-byte from data/interim/ at seed 42 -- so it is gitignored like every
# other regenerable corpus artefact. The PLAN is not: `sampling_plan.json`
# carries the template partition and the parameters the paper's methods section
# is written from, and it must be reviewable in a diff. If the plan changes
# without anyone noticing, the evaluation set silently changes with it.
# Note the un-ignore dance: line 15 ignores `data/processed/*` wholesale, and
# git will not descend into an ignored DIRECTORY, so the directory itself has to
# be re-included before a file inside it can be.
!data/processed/gold_candidates/
data/processed/gold_candidates/*
!data/processed/gold_candidates/sampling_plan.json

# Phase 10 silver labels. 9,302 rows, ~10 MB, and fully regenerable offline from
# data/interim/ with `python scripts/run_labeling.py` -- the same reasoning that
# keeps data/raw/ and data/interim/ out of the repo. The manifest and provenance
# ARE kept: they are the claims about what was produced, and a claim that cannot
# be diffed is a claim nobody checks. Same un-ignore dance as gold_candidates.
!data/processed/silver/
data/processed/silver/*/silver.jsonl

# Annotation-QA queue: regenerated with the labels, and 1.7 MB of it.
logs/review_queue.jsonl
logs/labeling_*.json
# Phase 14 per-configuration run logs. Not committed, for the same reason the
# labeling logs above are not: `reports/transformer.json` already carries every
# field of every one of these blocks, manifests included, so committing them
# duplicates the artifact rather than adding provenance. A sweep writes twelve
# of them (6 configurations x 2 splits) and they are pure scratch between runs.
#
# They are also where the training fingerprint -- a SHA-256 digest -- lands, and
# detect-secrets correctly flags any long hex string as a possible secret. Not
# committing them removes that false positive at the source instead of adding
# exceptions for it.
logs/transformer_*.json

# Phase 11 Potato projects. Regenerated from config/taxonomy.yaml by
# `python scripts/run_annotation.py --build`, so the generator is the artefact
# and the generated project is not. The annotators' RAW OUTPUT is a different
# matter: it is irreplaceable human work, but it is also the un-validated
# precursor of data/gold/, and the validated version IS committed. Keeping both
# would mean two copies of the same judgements that can disagree.
annotation/*/data/
annotation/*/annotation_output/
annotation/*/config.yaml
annotation/*/README.md

# Phase 11 adjudication worklist: derived from the two passes, regenerated by
# `run_annotation.py --agreement`.
logs/adjudication_*.jsonl

# Archived previous version
_legacy/

# Experiment tracking / logs
wandb/
logs/*.log
logs/cost_ledger.csv

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
# FUSE leaves these behind when an open file is deleted; 21 stale copies of
# live docs were committed before this line existed (Phase 33).
.fuse_hidden*
donations_inbox*.jsonl
consent_forms/

Claude outputs/
